# XTWINOPS 8: while the host turns window operations on, a program asks
# for a text area of so many rows and columns, which the host takes once.
# A parameter left out keeps that side, 0 takes the display's length on
# that side, and a later request replaces an earlier one. The request
# gets no reply, and the terminal keeps its size until the host resizes
# it. While window operations are off, the request is ignored (ctlseqs,
# XTWINOPS; INTERFACE-vtium.md, Font and window operations).
# spec: ADR-1000 window.resize
# capability: xtwinops-resize
size 10 4
send "\e[8;25;80t"
cmd grid-request
check
want test grid-request none
cmd window-ops;on=1
send "\e[8;25;80t"
cmd grid-request
cmd grid-request
send "\e[8;;80t\e[8;0t"
cmd grid-request
check
want test grid-request 25 80
want test grid-request none
want test grid-request display keep
want size 10x4
reply ""
